WEBVTT

00:10:59.507 --> 00:11:01.594
that casts them
in the best possible light.

00:11:01.618 --> 00:11:04.890
But you can overcome that problem
with situational questions.

00:11:04.914 --> 00:11:08.462
Instead of, "Tell me
about a time when," you ask,

00:11:08.486 --> 00:11:10.267
"What would you do if ... ?"

00:11:10.771 --> 00:11:12.101
Woman 1: What would you do

00:11:12.125 --> 00:11:14.474
if the superstar on your team
was about to quit?

00:11:14.498 --> 00:11:18.224
Man 1: What would you do if you saw
a senior executive yelling at a colleague?

00:11:18.248 --> 00:11:19.502
Woman 2: What would you do

00:11:19.526 --> 00:11:22.018
if all your colleagues
ate all the fruit salad?

00:11:23.675 --> 00:11:25.908
AG: Situational questions
are especially useful

00:11:25.932 --> 00:11:27.431
for forecasting potential,

00:11:27.455 --> 00:11:30.486
and for assessing leadership
and interpersonal skills.